A||||4||recluse||Front battery relocation (info & pics?)||||5||
Z||000000||recluse||10-28-2001||12:53 AM||||Considering a front battery relocation.  Can anyone tell me how difficult it is to mount, cost, and where to run the cable, and also does the battery get mounted under or above the spare?  And how hard is it to remove the spare if needed?  Pics would help alot, thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Pheagey||10-28-2001||01:50 AM||||ditto||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||10-28-2001||02:34 AM||||Did you try the search?  I know this has been gone over a lot in the past.  I don't know if there have been many pics, but it's a pretty straightforward deal.  Just run longer wires and mount it one way or another.  Some have put it on top of the spare, some have sunk it into the spare area into the radiator flow zone, some have mounted it where the spare tire jack goes, etc.  The difficulty, 4 on a scale of ten, only because you have to find a good route and mount the wire where it CAN'T rub through on anything.  Cost..depends on how you do it, who does it, etc.<P>There is a lot out there, use the search function.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||88CoupeV6||10-28-2001||08:35 AM||||Here is mine. I used #1gauge cable. I ran the + cable along side the fuel tank and grounded the - to the frame under the jack. I mounted the battery by flipping the spare upside down and putting the optima battery inside. I then just used the stock Tire holddown around the battery/tire. Yes you would have to remove the battery to get the spare out.  hope that helps<P>P.S. I only recommend the Optima battery as it will not vent gasses and can be mounted at any angle.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/battl.JPG"> ||||reg||3
Z||000004||Bazooka||10-28-2001||12:24 PM||||Recluse,   Its a Bi*ch getting the spare tire out of the "front well" with the battery in there. Plus with the archie battery tray, there are no "holddown" fasteners for the battery. Yeah, it just lays underneath the spare. Optima batteries are nice if you dont mind the $125 cost. Then again, if its mounted sideways, I'm not sure what the result would be when hitting a few potholes at 25 mph.<BR>******************************<BR>Originally posted by recluse:<BR>[B]Considering a front battery relocation.  Can anyone tell me how difficult it is to mount, cost, and where to run the cable, and also does the battery get mounted under or above the spare?  And how hard is it to remove the spare if needed?  Pics would help alot, thanks.<BR>**************************<P>||||reg||1
